project next 1
I need front end and backend work to start and anywhere from 30-50 router API integrations for a  comprehensive healthcare management system that will have the following:

-User Roles: Admins, Caregivers, Clients (or Agencies)
-Scheduling System: Calendar-based scheduling for caregivers and clients
-Billing & Invoicing: Automated payment processing and invoices
-Caregiver Management: Profiles, availability tracking, and assignment
-Secure Login & Authentication: User-specific dashboards
-Electronic Visit Verification (EVV): GPS-based check-in/check-out for caregivers
-Reporting & Analytics: Insights for agencies

For tech stack (this is just some recommendation)
Frontend (User Interface)
React.js / Tailwind CSS / Next.js

Backend (Server & Logic)
Node.js with Express.js (Handles API requests efficiently)
NestJS (Optional for structured backend development)

Database
PostgreSQL (Relational database for structured data like users, payments, schedules)
Redis (For caching frequently accessed data)

Authentication & Security
JWT (JSON Web Tokens) (For secure user authentication)
OAuth 2.0 (For QuickBooks & Google Calendar integration)
AWS Cognito or Firebase Auth (For scalable authentication)

Third-Party Integrations
QuickBooks API (For billing & invoicing)
Google Calendar API (For scheduling & reminders)
Stripe/PayPal (For payments processing)
Twilio (For SMS reminders & caregiver communication)
Hosting & Deployment
AWS (Amazon Web Services) (Scalability & reliability)
Docker & Kubernetes (For managing deployment)

Tech Stack for Mobile App
React Native (Cross-platform for both iOS & Android)
Expo (For faster development and easier testing)
Firebase or AWS Amplify (For real-time sync & notifications)
SQLite or RealmDB (For offline functionality)
Features for Mobile App
✅ Caregiver & Client Dashboards (Schedules, tasks, notifications)
✅ Scheduling & Calendar Sync (With Google Calendar API)
✅ GPS Tracking & Check-in/Check-out (For Electronic Visit Verification)
✅ Billing & Payment Integration (QuickBooks, Stripe, etc.)
✅ Push Notifications & Reminders (For appointments & updates)

This website/App will essentially be a caregiver/clients management system for hospitals and healthcare facilities. If you have experience in back end development that will help as well.

















project: 3

AI-Powered Data Analysis Dashboard - Full Stack Development

We are building a modern, AI-powered data analysis dashboard designed to make complex data exploration more accessible to domain experts with limited computational expertise. The app enables users to upload datasets and guide the analysis through a conversational interface with AI.

Key Features
1. Chat Interface
- Streaming conversational AI interactions (supporting both AsyncOpenAI and non-async response)
- Model will return various data structures. So must support rich reply formats: text, tables (rendered on front end), charts (rendered on front end), and images.
- Chat history features: rename, delete, and export previous sessions.

2. File Management
Upload system for datasets (e.g., CSV, Excel).

3. Data Analysis Panel
- Terminal/Code Section: Displays AI-generated scripts used in analysis with syntax highlighting and standard monospaced formatting.
- Plots Tab: Shows most recent visualizations with the ability to scroll through history. Expandable to view multiple plots simultaneously.
- Tables Tab: Tabular data with sample indexing, standardized dimensions, and scrollable for large datasets.

4. UI Customization
- Tabs are draggable, expandable, and rearrangeable.
- Layout supports vertical, horizontal, and overlay alignments for flexible multi-view workflows.
- Light/dark theme toggle in settings.

5. Interoperability
- AI model will return text stream along with any raw table, image, and data that must be organized into the appropriate section and rendered in the front-end

This project is ideal for a full-stack developer experienced with modern frameworks (React, Next.js, Node.js, etc.) and a strong understanding of dynamic frontends paired with AI integrations. You'll be working directly from finalized designs to bring the interface to life.


Project 4: SaaS

CRM and Job Scheduling Tool for Service Workers

Project goal
Develop a lightweight CRM combined with a job scheduling tool tailored for service industry workers such as plumbers, electricians, and HVAC technicians.

Scope of work
- Design and implement a lite CRM system to track customer info, link clients to projects, and manage deadlines.
- Develop a simple job scheduling and dispatch module that allows assigning jobs to employees, sending notifications, and tracking job status.
- Create a platform that integrates both CRM and job scheduling features with user-friendly interfaces suitable for both desktop and mobile use.


Technical requirements
- The system should be web-based with a responsive design for desktop and mobile app support for field staff.
- Ensure compatibility with major browsers and mobile operating systems.
- Implement security measures to protect client and job data.

Design preferences
User interface should be simple, clean, and easy to navigate, reflecting the tool's purpose and functionality. Modern SaaS design but with minimal fields and things to see per page.

Additional information
- The app should function similarly to Google Calendar but with enhanced features for service industry needs, including job notes, photo attachments, and automatic notifications.

Software Architecture & Design


🔁 Update/Delete data sekalian refresh cache

🧠 Integrasi Statistik/AI di .NET Microservice

🔐 JWT Auth & Role-based Access

💅 Frontend polish: grafik, UI, SEO

📈 Integrasi GraphQL, Webhooks, Notifikasi real-time

✅ Atau integrasi ke frontend (simpan token)

-Integrasi di frontend → simpan token (misal localStorage)
-Opsional: Role-based Access (admin, user)


